cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ViTeX-Bench: Benchmarking High Fidelity Video Scene Text Editing"
message: "If you use ViTeX-Bench, please cite the accompanying paper."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Anonymous"
abstract: >
  ViTeX-Bench is a benchmark suite for faithful and temporally consistent
  video scene text editing. It defines a thirteen-metric protocol over
  three axes (text correctness, visual quality, and edit locality) on a
  permanently frozen 157-clip evaluation split, and ships an open
  reference model (ViTeX-Edit-14B) anchored under the same protocol.
keywords:
  - video editing
  - scene text editing
  - benchmark
license: Apache-2.0
preferred-citation:
  type: conference-paper
  title: "ViTeX-Bench: Benchmarking High Fidelity Video Scene Text Editing"
  authors:
    - name: "Anonymous"
  collection-title: "Submitted to NeurIPS 2026 Datasets and Benchmarks Track"
  year: 2026
  notes: "Author list and DOI updated after deanonymization."
